course: dictionary
lesson: 13119
title: Flotation and floating
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Flotation means floating, or how well something stays on top of water. You can hear the word float inside it, so if you know float, you are already most of the way there. «The old wooden raft has good flotation, so it stays on top of the lake.» The clue is stays on top: that tells you flotation is about floating.
explain: A flotation device is something that helps you float. «Mum made me put on a flotation device before I went in the pool.» Life jackets and armbands are flotation devices. A flotation aid means the same kind of thing.
explain: In money news, flotation means something different. «The company's flotation on the stock market was today.» The clue is the word first: a flotation is when a company sells shares to the public for the very first time. Always check the words around it to see which meaning fits.
fact: Flotation means floating, or the ability to stay on top of water.
fact: A flotation device helps you float, like a life jacket or armbands.
fact: In money news, a flotation is when a company first sells shares to the public on the stock market.
fact: Float to live is a water safety rule: if you get tired in water, lie on your back, stay calm and float.
fact: Flotation is a noun, and it comes from the verb float.
exercise: «The boat has good flotation, so it stays on top of the water.» What does flotation mean here? | Sinking to the bottom | Painting the boat | *Ability to float on water | Going very fast
exercise: Which of these is a flotation device? | A pile of sand | A heavy iron anchor | A dry pencil | *A life jacket
exercise: «The company's flotation on the stock market was today.» What does flotation mean here? | *A company's first sale of shares to the public | A new kind of swimming costume | A boat sinking in a storm | A bank holiday
test: You get tired while swimming in a lake. What does the water safety rule float to live tell you to do? | Swim straight to the far side at once | Panic and kick as hard as you can | *Lie on your back, stay calm and float | Shout and wave at the sky
test: Flotation is a noun. Which word is the verb it comes from? | Flow | *Float | Flat | Flute
exam: A boy says flotation means pretty flowers. Why is he wrong? | Flotation means the colour of the sea | *Flotation means floating on water, not flowers | Flotation means flowers that grow in ponds | Flotation means a flower shop
